eated_at":"2026-01-22T00:48:44Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T15:09:24Z","closed_at":"2026-01-27T15:09:24Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"- *Related to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/115232.*\n\n### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.6.rc2\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.rc (76addfff1) - Fedora Linux 43 (KDE Plasma Desktop Edition) on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5090 (nvidia; 580.119.02) - AMD Ryzen 9 9950X3D 16-Core Processor (32 threads) - 62.33 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nEngine Compilation Configuration Editor does not detect Navigation 2D being unused.\n\nThis can be reproduced on the [3D platformer demo](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/tree/master/3d/platformer), or even on an empty project. Neither use 2D navigation functionality, but autodetection will still consider it as if it was used somewhere.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Open **Project > Tools > Engine Compilation Configuration Editor** in the editor.\n- Click **Detect from Project** and confirm the dialog.\n- Notice that 2D navigation is still enabled, even though 3D navigation is disabled.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/tree/master/3d/platformer","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.c